@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string with normal string conversion, joins them with ``sep`` and writes them followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+Unlike print, ``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, process markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written literally.
+
+By default ``out`` applies highlighting, which you can turn off with ``highlight=False``, or defer to the Console setting with ``highlight=None``. You can also apply a basic ``style``.
+
+
